From: Hang Nan <2122295973@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:39:05 +0200
Subject: power_supply: serialize property access with unregister
Git-commit: 9f7f7a85945156d5c7626390a8c46d43d5159abc
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

Extend 5b4bd13e0552 ("power: supply: core: prevent unregistering a power
supply while a callback runs") fix to also cover the get and set property
hooks.

This has been tested with a small out-of-tree module registering a
supply whose get property function caches its drv_data pointer and then
sleeps 300 ms, while the module's main thread calls power_supply_unregister()
and then frees that drv_data:

unpatched:  unregister() returns after       78 us
            callback then reads drv_data   0x6b6b6b6b  (slub poison)
            => the driver callback read freed memory

patched:    unregister() returns after   302549 us  (the 300 ms callback)
            callback then reads drv_data   0x12345678  (intact)
            => power_supply_unregister() waits for the in-flight callback

The lock is taken in the wrappers rather than in the helper so that the
_direct() variants stay lockless: a caller that has to read its own
supply from within a callback uses those, and rwsem read locking is not
recursive once a writer is waiting.

Fixes: bc1540561c9e ("power_supply: Add API for safe access of power supply function attrs")
Fixes: 5b4bd13e0552 ("power: supply: core: prevent unregistering a power supply while a callback runs")
Signed-off-by: Hang Nan <2122295973@qq.com>
[massively trim down AI commit message and comments]
Signed-off-by: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c b/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c
index c3f3c70b9449..2e1058bd24c8 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c
@@ -1422,6 +1422,12 @@ static int __power_supply_get_property(struct power_supply *psy, enum power_supp
 int power_supply_get_property(struct power_supply *psy, enum power_supply_property psp,
 			      union power_supply_propval *val)
 {
+	/* Protect driver data from being free'd */
+	guard(rwsem_read)(&psy->epc_sem);
+
+	if (psy->removing)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	return __power_supply_get_property(psy, psp, val, true);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(power_supply_get_property);
@@ -1479,6 +1485,12 @@ static int __power_supply_set_property(struct power_supply *psy, enum power_supp
 int power_supply_set_property(struct power_supply *psy, enum power_supply_property psp,
 			      const union power_supply_propval *val)
 {
+	/* Protect driver data from being free'd */
+	guard(rwsem_read)(&psy->epc_sem);
+
+	if (psy->removing)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	return __power_supply_set_property(psy, psp, val, true);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(power_supply_set_property);

